  <h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Common Error</th><th>Correction</th></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Knees extend beyond toes</td><td>Bend knees only slightly — keep knee tips vertically within the toes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Puffing chest/belly</td><td>Relax the chest, keep the abdomen natural, do not deliberately push it out</td></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Sticking out buttocks</td><td>Tailbone centered, imagine sitting on a balloon chair</td></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Shrugging shoulders</td><td>Sink shoulders, drop elbows; armpit balloon imagery helps relaxation</td></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Arms pressed flat against body</td><td>Hold balloons under armpits, prop arms slightly away from the body</td></tr>
    <tr><td>❌ Forceful breath-holding</td><td>Inhale and exhale through the nose, naturally and silently</td></tr>
  </table>

  ---

  <h2>Common Reactions and Sensations</h2>
  <p>Beginners may experience the following reactions when practicing Wu Chi. These are all <strong>normal</strong>:</p>
  <ul class="key-points">
    <li>Soreness, numbness, or trembling in the legs — muscles adapting to a new load</li>
    <li>Sweating — even without movement, internal energy is at work</li>
    <li>Tingling, warmth, swelling, or numbness in the fingers — signs of chi flow</li>
    <li>Slight swaying of the body — normal internal movement</li>
    <li>Feeling exhausted — common in the beginning; with persistence, this transforms into abundant energy</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout callout-warn">
    <h4>⚠️ Caution</h4>
    <p>If you feel <strong>dizzy or overheated</strong>, stop immediately and sit down to rest. Do not push through.
    Start with 3-5 minutes and gradually increase the duration.</p>
  </div>

  ---

  <h2>Quick Reference Card</h2>
  <div class="cheatsheet">
    <h4>🧍 Wu Chi — One-Page Quick Reference</h4>
    <dl>
      <dt>Feet</dt><dd>Shoulder-width apart, toes forward, weight even</dd>
      <dt>Knees</dt><dd>Slightly bent, not beyond toes</dd>
      <dt>Body</dt><dd>Spine straight, sitting-not-sitting (balloon chair), no puffing chest or buttocks</dd>
      <dt>Arms</dt><dd>Hanging naturally, armpit balloons, arms slightly propped</dd>
      <dt>Head</dt><dd>Head suspended, gaze forward, chin slightly tucked</dd>
      <dt>Breath</dt><dd>Nasal breathing, natural, deep, and silent</dd>
      <dt>Duration</dt><dd>Start with 3-5 minutes, gradually increase to 20 minutes</dd>
      <dt>Flow</dt><dd>Warm-up (knee rotations) → Wu Chi → Cool-down (hip rotations)</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

